/** @page xmlwebdavguide WebDAV Servers and Clients

    @tableofcontents

    The user modules delivered with the xml module implement WebDAV
    (<a href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/rfc/rfc4918">RFC 4918</a>) servers for the %Qore \c HttpServer and WebDAV
    clients.

    @section xmlwebdavmodules Choosing a Module

    |!Task|!Module|!Main classes
    |Serve a directory tree, or a custom resource store, over WebDAV|\
        @ref webdavhandlerintro "WebDavHandler"|@ref WebDavHandler::FsWebDavHandler "FsWebDavHandler", \
        @ref WebDavHandler::AbstractWebDavHandler "AbstractWebDavHandler"
    |Access a WebDAV server (asynchronous I/O, HTTP/3, HTTP/2 or HTTP/1.1; recommended)|\
        @ref webdavclientiointro "WebDavClientIo"|@ref WebDavClientIo::WebDavClientIo "WebDavClientIo"
    |Access a WebDAV server with the synchronous \c HTTPClient API|\
        @ref webdavclientintro "WebDavClient"|@ref WebDavClient::WebDavClient "WebDavClient"
    |Access WebDAV resources through the data provider API (list, get, put, delete, mkdir, copy, move)|\
        @ref webdavclientdataproviderintro "WebDavClientDataProvider"|\
        @ref WebDavClientDataProvider::WebDavClientDataProvider "WebDavClientDataProvider"

    The clients provide the same API method for method, and connection objects for them are registered with the
    \c webdav and \c webdavs (@ref WebDavClient::WebDavClient "WebDavClient") and \c webdavio and \c webdavios (@ref WebDavClientIo::WebDavClientIo "WebDavClientIo") schemes.

    @section xmlwebdavserver WebDAV Server

    @ref WebDavHandler::FsWebDavHandler "FsWebDavHandler" serves a directory tree; custom resource stores subclass @ref WebDavHandler::AbstractWebDavHandler "AbstractWebDavHandler". Both
    advertise WebDAV compliance classes 1 and 2 (<tt>DAV: 1,2</tt>) and accept the \c OPTIONS, \c GET, \c HEAD,
    \c POST, \c PUT, \c DELETE, \c MKCOL, \c COPY, \c MOVE, \c PROPFIND, \c PROPPATCH, \c LOCK and \c UNLOCK
    methods.

    |!Feature|!Behavior
    |Properties|dead properties are stored by a property handler: in memory (@ref WebDavHandler::InMemoryWebDavPropertyHandler "InMemoryWebDavPropertyHandler") or \
        in a JSON file (@ref WebDavHandler::FileWebDavPropertyHandler "FileWebDavPropertyHandler"); \c COPY and \c MOVE carry a resource's properties, and \
        replace those of an overwritten destination
    |Locks|exclusive and shared write locks with depth 0 or infinity, timeouts, refresh and \c UNLOCK anywhere in \
        the lock's scope (RFC 4918 sections 9.10 and 9.11), kept by a lock handler (in memory, \
        @ref WebDavHandler::InMemoryWebDavLockHandler "InMemoryWebDavLockHandler", by default; locks are lost when the server restarts)
    |Lock enforcement|every method that changes a resource requires the tokens of the locks that apply to it, \
        including depth-infinity locks of its ancestors and the locks below a collection that is deleted, moved or \
        replaced; a missing token gives <tt>423 Locked</tt> with \c DAV:lock-token-submitted
    |Conditional requests|the \c If header (RFC 4918 section 10.4: tagged and untagged lists, \c Not, lock tokens \
        and entity tags) is evaluated for every method; a false condition gives <tt>412 Precondition Failed</tt>
    |Entity tags|quoted strings derived from the file's inode, size and modification time
    |COPY and MOVE|\c Depth: 0 copies a collection without its members; 201 for a new and 204 for a replaced \
        destination (RFC 4918 section 9.8.5)
    |Request bodies|streamed \c PUT and \c POST bodies over HTTP/1.1, HTTP/2 and HTTP/3; a body larger than the \
        server's maximum request body size gives <tt>413 Content Too Large</tt>, and a body that stops arriving \
        gives <tt>408 Request Timeout</tt>

    @subsection xmlwebdavconformance Conformance

    @ref WebDavHandler::FsWebDavHandler "FsWebDavHandler" passes all five suites of the <a href="https://notroj.github.io/litmus/">litmus</a> WebDAV
    compliance test: basic (16/16), copymove (13/13), props (33/33), locks (40/40) and http (4/4). The module's
    test suite runs litmus in CI.

    @section xmlwebdavclient WebDAV Clients

    The clients list collections (\c list(), \c propfind()), transfer resources (\c get(), \c put()), manage
    collections and resources (\c mkcol(), \c del(), \c copyResource(), \c moveResource(), \c exists()), and lock
    resources (\c lock(), \c unlock()). The helper methods do not send \c If headers: to change a resource that
    is locked, send the request with an <tt>If: (&lt;lock-token&gt;)</tt> header through the underlying HTTP client
    API.

    @section xmlwebdavexamples Examples

    See @ref xmlcookbookwebdav "the cookbook" for a server and client example.
*/
